description:
## Goal

Make runtime demand ordinary spreadsheet-style reactive cells and delete the whole-cone fixpoint engine. The semantic unit of work and the scheduled unit of work must be the same: a changed demand cell wakes only the formulas that read it.

## Fresh signal (release compiler, 2026-08-24)

fixtures2/behavior/enum_take_drop_split.fz:

- 660 ms compile session;
- 237 unique backend activation keys / 239 backend executables;
- six large demand settlements: 197 members x4, then 237 members x2;
- 6,540 member derivations, while the final 237-member solution needs 1,246;
- external_members=0 throughout.

fixtures2/behavior/fz_f98_range_map_converges.fz:

- 103 ms for four executable source lines;
- 59 unique backend activation keys / 61 backend executables;
- six large demand settlements: 55 members x4, then 59 members x2;
- 1,566 member derivations, while the final 59-member solution needs 277;
- external_members=0 throughout.

The repeated equal-size settlements are not displaced-external churn. produce_runtime_demand_product solves the graph, discovers callable-flow resolutions from that solution, records them in actual_flow_edges, discards the solution, and restarts from bottom. Edge growth without member growth is explicitly accepted by DemandConeRetryGuard.

## Core modeling error

ProductKey::RuntimeDemand(E) claims one-executable ownership, while ExecutableRuntimeDemand collapses several independently moving concepts:

- return demand;
- input demand per semantic slot;
- local value demand;
- call argument/capture demand;
- callable surfaces and resolved callable-flow edges;
- caller-to-target return and boundary-input contributions.

Those facts move in different directions. Combining them into one product invents a program-sized dependency component and forces hand-written dirty indexes, session contribution stores, atomic cone publication, invalidation waves, and topology-restart logic.

## Strategy

After fz-kdt.34 supplies generic cyclic quiescence:

1. Build immutable demand equations from ExecutableFacts; do not repeatedly walk a root/cone to rediscover formulas.
2. Give independently moving demand projections and source-to-target contributions exact fact/cell identities.
3. Let the authoritative contribution store perform monotone joins, as activation-input contributions already do.
4. Record exact reads so a changed cell wakes only formulas that consume it.
5. Publish callable-flow edges as ordinary monotone topology facts. Adding an edge installs its dependency and evaluates only the new affected frontier; standing demand values remain intact.
6. Gate artifact/transport consumers on the generic quiescent epoch plus the exact cells they read.
7. Delete the bespoke solver and side channels.

No stratification pass, anchor ordering, leaf seeding, cone cap, chunking heuristic, replay cache, or fixture-specific shortcut belongs in the design.

## Required deletions

- collect_demand_cone
- settle_demand_cone
- DemandConeRetryGuard
- DemandGraph / SettledDemandCone
- actual_flow_edges
- demand-specific edge-reader/dirty indexes
- PullSession return/input demand contribution and contributor maps
- replace_settled_*_demand_contributions / recompute_*_demand
- whole-cone demand memo publication and its bespoke invalidation paths
- cone settlement telemetry once replacement cell telemetry proves the stronger invariant

## Telemetry acceptance

For both named fixtures and a small dynamic-callable reproducer:

- every non-initial demand-formula evaluation names at least one dependency revision it had not observed;
- unchanged output produces zero reader wakes;
- topology growth produces zero value resets and zero replayed settled regions;
- every demand cell settles once per quiescent epoch;
- no whole-graph scans occur;
- an incremental edit evaluates only the changed cell's transitive reader closure;
- work counts are identical across repeated runs;
- behavior remains byte-correct on interp, run, and build.

Use work counts, not wall-clock thresholds.

## Documentation

Replace the current semantic-fixpoint description of whole-cone Kleene settlement with the reactive-cell and quiescent-epoch invariant. Document what disappeared as well as what replaced it.
